From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mksquashfs: run on a camera with 45 MB of RAM

mksquashfs refuses to start below 64 MB of physical memory ("requires more
physical memory than is available"), whatever -mem says. The TECKIN TC100 has
about 45 MB for Linux, and the 3.0 flash install builds the 1 MB squashfs of the
camera's own vendor libraries on the camera. 32 MB is plenty for that (-mem 8M).

--- a/squashfs-tools/mksquashfs.h
+++ b/squashfs-tools/mksquashfs.h
@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@
  * Lowest amount of physical memory considered viable for Mksquashfs
  * to run in Mbytes
  */
-#define SQUASHFS_LOWMEM 64
+#define SQUASHFS_LOWMEM 32
 
 /* offset of data in compressed metadata blocks (allowing room for
  * compressed size */
